    "raw": "\\*Data estimated 300-585 K. \nPhase change: 585 K, melting point of $As_{2}S_{3}$ ; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 6.874$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n$$\n\\begin{array}{l} 2 9 8. 1 5 - 5 8 5 \\mathrm{K}: \\quad \\mathrm{Cp} ^ {\\circ} = 2 8. 9 0 3 + 3. 1 3 2 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} - 1. 8 2 8 \\times 1 0 ^ {5} \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 2} \\\\ \\mathrm{H} ^ {0} - \\mathrm{H} _ {2 9 8} ^ {0} = 2 8. 9 0 3 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} + 1. 5 6 6 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 1. 8 2 8 \\times 1 0 ^ {2} \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} - 9. 3 7 0 \\\\ 5 8 5 - 8 5 0 \\mathrm{K}: \\quad \\mathrm{Cp} ^ {\\circ} = 3 1. 1 7 8 + 9. 5 8 6 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} + 3 0. 0 3 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {5} \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 2} \\\\ \\mathrm{H} ^ {\\circ} - \\mathrm{H} _ {2 9 8} ^ {\\circ} = 3 1. 1 7 8 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} + 4. 7 9 3 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} - 3 0. 0 3 0 \\times 1 0 ^ {2} \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} + 0. 5 1 5 \\\\ \\end{array}\n$$\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n$$\n\\begin{array}{l} 2 9 8. 1 5 - 5 8 5 \\mathrm{K}: \\quad \\Delta \\mathrm{Hr} ^ {\\circ} = - 6 9. 6 2 9 + 5. 0 0 6 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} - 0. 0 5 6 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 5 5. 5 5 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} \\\\ \\Delta G r ^ {\\circ} = - 6 9. 6 2 9 - 5. 0 0 6 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{TlnT} + 0. 0 5 6 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} + 2 7. 7 7 5 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} + 9 3. 6 3 8 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} \\\\ 5 8 5 - 8 5 0 \\mathrm{K}: \\quad \\Delta \\mathrm{Hr} ^ {\\circ} = - 5 9. 7 4 4 + 7. 2 8 1 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} + 3. 1 7 1 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} - 3 1 3 0. 2 5 0 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} \\\\ \\Delta \\mathrm{Gr} ^ {\\circ} = - 5 9. 7 4 4 - 7. 2 8 1 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{TlnT} - 3. 1 7 1 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 6} \\mathrm{T} ^ {2} - 1 5 6 5. 1 2 5 \\mathrm{T} ^ {- 1} + 9 7. 7 7 9 \\times 1 0 ^ {- 3} \\mathrm{T} \\\\ \\end{array}\n$$\nSources: Enthalpy of formation from Johnson (55). Low-temperature heat capacities and entropy at 298 K from Romanovskii (102). Data 300-585 K estimated. Data 585-850 K from Mah (73). ",
